Final Conclusion
All four event-handling techniques can perform the same currency conversion operation. Lambda expressions are suitable for short event handlers, while named inner classes provide better organization for complex event logic. Method references provide a concise way to connect existing methods. A shared Swing Action is the most suitable approach when the same operation must be triggered by buttons, menu items and keyboard shortcuts because it allows the application to reuse one action object.
